    "  - Description of the variables most relevant to this project\n",
    "  - Descriptions of any shortcomings this dataset has with repsect to the project\n",
    "- Dataset #2\n",
    "  - E-commerce Customer Behaviour Dataset\n",
    "  - https://www.kaggle.com/code/paulsamuelwe/eda-predictive-analysis-on-e-commerce-dataset\n",
    "  - Number of Observations: 50 \n",
    "  - Number of Variables: 9 \n",
    "  - Description of the Variables Most Relevant to this Project: Description of the variables most relevant to this project: The E-Commerce Customer Behavior Dataset is relevant to our project as it provides a demographic context of the customers visiting the page. We can separate the key variables we will use to predict purchasing patterns into purchasing power/region with annual income, age, and location and demographic data of the individuals through purchase history and browsing history. Using the time on site variable, we can measure the user’s total engagement addressing our hypothesis of the correlation between time spent and purchasing probability. \n",
    "  - Descriptions of any shortcomings this dataset has with repsect to the project: \n",
    "Descriptions of any shortcomings this dataset has with respect to the project: Despite the strengths of this dataset, it comes with limitations. It lacks user tracking of their interactions with the product other than the time spent on the page. Additionally, the dataset does not include if users add or remove items from their cart.\n",
    "Each dataset deserves either a set of bullet points as above or a few sentences if you prefer that method.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you plan to use multiple datasets, add a few sentences about how you plan to combine these datasets. \n",
    
    "Since the datasets share different user sets and different metrics, each dataset will serve their own purpose. Dataset #1 includes information about user behaviors through duration, bounce rate, page values, etc. whereas Dataset #2 has information regarding demographic information of the user from their income, age, and region. With this information, we will compare the models to see how user engagement and demographics may influence purchase decisions in tandem. \n",
   ]
